WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.740
A construction site never stands still.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.720
Humanoid robots could soon carry
materials through buildings like this one.

00:00:23.151 --> 00:00:28.231
But on a busy site, loads swing, workers
carry long pipes, and machines turn.

00:00:30.721 --> 00:00:35.661
Being struck by an object is one of the
leading causes of death in construction.

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:46.092
The robot carries its load up ramps and
stairs, and across wet floors and debris.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.593
When something hangs
in its path, it squats,

00:00:56.593 --> 00:00:58.763
twists or bends, and keeps walking.

00:01:06.085 --> 00:01:08.165
Moving hazards need timing.

00:01:08.165 --> 00:01:12.885
ForeSite looks a few seconds ahead and
chooses how to move, and when to go.

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:25.998
Without ForeSite, a hit can knock the
robot over and make it drop its load.

00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:29.668
With ForeSite, it waits
and passes behind the load.

00:01:33.903 --> 00:01:36.093
ForeSite links a walking policy

00:01:36.093 --> 00:01:40.703
and a safety filter through a planner
that chooses posture and speed together.

00:01:46.511 --> 00:01:47.711
ForeSite.

00:01:47.711 --> 00:01:49.131
Knowing how to move, and when to go.
